    >>> torch.fft.fft(t)
    tensor([ 6.+0.j, -2.+2.j, -2.+0.j, -2.-2.j])

    Notice that the symmetric element ``T[-1] == T[1].conj()`` is omitted.
    At the Nyquist frequency ``T[-2] == T[2]`` is it's own symmetric pair,
    and therefore must always be real-valued.

